# Vector-2D: a 2-component 32-bit-float vector. Pure float math. `add` / `subtract` combine (it wears `addition` and `subtraction`), `scale` by a scalar, `dot` is the scalar product, `cross` the scalar (z-component) cross product, `magnitude` the norm, `normalize` the unit vector, `distance` the gap.

mark unstable

load @term/base/float
  find square-root

load @term/base/arithmetic
  find addition
  find subtraction

form vector-2
  link x, like float
  link y, like float

  wear addition
    task add
      take self
      take other, like vector-2
      like vector-2
      send back
        make vector-2
          bind x
            call add
              read self/x
              read other/x
          bind y
            call add
              read self/y
              read other/y

  wear subtraction
    task subtract
      take self
      take other, like vector-2
      like vector-2
      send back
        make vector-2
          bind x
            call subtract
              read self/x
              read other/x
          bind y
            call subtract
              read self/y
              read other/y

  # the names before `add` reached a vector (note/term/plan/decisions-2026-10.md, D5), kept for one release
  task plus
    take self
    take other, like vector-2
    like vector-2
    mark deprecated
    back self/add(other)

  task minus
    take self
    take other, like vector-2
    like vector-2
    mark deprecated
    back self/subtract(other)

  task scale
    take self
    take factor, like float
    like vector-2
    send back
      make vector-2
        bind x
          call multiply
            read self/x
            read factor
        bind y
          call multiply
            read self/y
            read factor

  task dot
    take self
    take other, like vector-2
    like float
    send back
      call add
        call multiply
          read self/x
          read other/x
        call multiply
          read self/y
          read other/y

  task cross
    take self
    take other, like vector-2
    like float
    send back
      call subtract
        call multiply
          read self/x
          read other/y
        call multiply
          read self/y
          read other/x

  # the norm: `magnitude`, since a collection's `length` counts its items (note/term/plan/decisions-2026-10.md, D2)
  task magnitude
    take self
    like float
    send back
      call square-root
        call dot
          read self
          read self

  # the older name of `magnitude`, kept one release
  task length
    take self
    like float
    mark deprecated
    back magnitude(self)

  task normalize
    take self
    like vector-2
    save magnitude
      call magnitude
        read self
    send back
      make vector-2
        bind x
          call divide
            read self/x
            read magnitude
        bind y
          call divide
            read self/y
            read magnitude

  task distance
    take self
    take other, like vector-2
    like float
    send back
      call magnitude
        call minus
          read self
          read other

task make-vector-2
  take x, like float
  take y, like float
  like vector-2
  send back
    make vector-2
      bind x, read x
      bind y, read y
